// Added after the 2026-09-22 adversarial variant pass; see docs/DECISIONS.md.
//#ASSERT TRUE : P27_EdgeMemoriesTrackInputs
//#ASSERT TRUE : P28_AbortClearedOnAcceptedStart
// P29-P31 derive the deadline from the threshold input, the prior timer and the
// completion levels only; xTimeoutReached never gates a check. The deadline
// "prevTimer+1 >= N" is written overflow-free as "prev < 65535 AND prev >= N-1";
// From initialization, prev never exceeds 65534: N=0 clears the timer,
// and any positive UINT threshold expires before another increment can reach 65535.
// The prev=65535 branches are outside this reachable-state proof; they do not
// establish behavior for injected state or cross-tool overflow equivalence.
//#ASSERT TRUE : P29_NoEarlyExpiration
//#ASSERT TRUE : P30_DeadlineObligation
//#ASSERT TRUE : P31_WaitingCallCountsOne
// P32 added after the 2026-09-26 adversarial round (plans/plc-adversarial-r2):
// a threshold-switched-to-zero variant that froze the prior timer passed every
// then-shipped layer. The obligation is derived from the contract sentence
// "Zero disables counting and keeps timer zero", not from derived signals.
// The reset-acceptance edge (contract C3) is native-only: at end of cycle the
// edge memory is already committed to this scan's input, so a single-state
// assertion cannot reference the previous scan's input, and the one temp that
// encodes it (xResetRise) is exactly what an edge-to-level mutant redefines.
//#ASSERT TRUE : P32_ZeroThresholdKeepsTimerZero